{"version" 2 "boxes" [{"id" "ascii_shape_circles" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root"} "name" "Six circles per cell" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [380.0 60.0 300.0 100.0] "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "ascii_shape_circles_notes_.md" "inline" "# Six circles per cell\n\nFive characters as the matcher sees them: six inner sampling circles (orange) give each character its six numbers; the outer ones (blue) feed directional contrast.\n"} "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "ascii_shape_circles_code_.kt" "inline" "// Five glyphs as the matcher sees them, 10x up: the cell in gray, its six circles in orange,\n// and the six just outside it in blue.\nval ascii = ShapeAscii()\nval k = 10.0\nfun circle(cx: Double, cy: Double, r: Double) = fline {\n    for (i in 0..48) {\n        val a = 2 * PI * i / 48\n        if (i == 0) moveTo(cx + r * cos(a), cy + r * sin(a)) else lineTo(cx + r * cos(a), cy + r * sin(a))\n    }\n}\nval circles = ascii.samplingCircles()\nval panels =\n    \"TL/o@\"\n        .map { ch ->\n            val i = ascii.glyphs.indexOf(ch)\n            // pad the cell so the outer circles fit, then draw the circles over it\n            val pad = ascii.cellWidth\n            val cell = ascii.glyphImg(i).pad(pad, Border.ZERO)\n            val inner =\n                circles.take(6).map { (x, y, r) ->\n                    circle(x + pad, y + pad, r).apply { color = Vec4(1f, 0.55f, 0.1f, 1f) }\n                }\n            val outer =\n                circles.drop(6).map { (x, y, r) ->\n                    circle(x + pad, y + pad, r).apply { color = Vec4(0.3f, 0.6f, 1f, 1f) }\n                }\n            val w = ascii.cellWidth.toDouble()\n            val h = ascii.cellHeight.toDouble()\n            val box = fline {\n                moveTo(pad, pad)\n                lineTo(pad + w, pad)\n                lineTo(pad + w, pad + h)\n                lineTo(pad, pad + h)\n                lineTo(pad, pad)\n            }\n            box.color = Vec4(0.5f, 0.5f, 0.5f, 1f)\n            \"'$ch'\" to cell.drawFLines(inner + outer + box, scale = k, thickness = 2.0)\n        }\nshowImgGrid(*panels.toTypedArray(), columns = 5, cellSide = 200)\n"}}} {"id" "ascii_shape_sphere" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root"} "name" "Lit sphere" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [720.0 60.0 300.0 100.0] "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "ascii_shape_sphere_notes_.md" "inline" "# A lit sphere\n\nShading by brightness ramp vs by shape. The method suits light marks on a dark ground.\n"} "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "ascii_shape_sphere_code_.kt" "inline" "// A lit sphere on black, shaded by hand: brightness is the cosine between the surface normal and a light.\nval scene =\n    Img.generate(300, 240) { x, y ->\n        val nx = (x - 150) / 100.0\n        val ny = (y - 120) / 100.0\n        val r2 = nx * nx + ny * ny\n        if (r2 < 1) {\n            val nz = sqrt(1 - r2)\n            (-0.5 * nx - 0.6 * ny + 0.62 * nz).coerceAtLeast(0.0).toFloat()\n        } else 0f\n    }\nval ascii = ShapeAscii()\nshowAscii(\n    \"brightness\" to ascii.convert(scene, 40, shape = false),\n    \"shape, contrast 2\" to ascii.convert(scene, 40, contrast = 2.0),\n    cellSide = 420,\n)\n"}}} {"id" "ascii_shape_shapes" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root"} "name" "Brightness vs shape" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 60.0 300.0 100.0] "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "ascii_shape_shapes_notes_.md" "inline" "# Shape-aware ASCII\n\nThe same FLine drawing as characters twice: picked by brightness alone (left) and by where the light falls in each cell (right), after Alex Harri's essay https://alexharri.com/blog/ascii-rendering. Run it; try `contrast = 3.0` in the second `convert`. Docs: ascii_shape.md.\n"} "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "ascii_shape_shapes_code_.kt" "inline" "// Three outlines and a filled disc, drawn white on black.\nfun ring(cx: Double, cy: Double, r: Double, sides: Int, turn: Double = 0.0) = fline {\n    for (i in 0..sides) {\n        val a = turn + 2 * PI * i / sides\n        if (i == 0) moveTo(cx + r * cos(a), cy + r * sin(a)) else lineTo(cx + r * cos(a), cy + r * sin(a))\n    }\n    thickness = 6.0\n}\nval disc = ring(360.0, 100.0, 55.0, 64).apply { filled = true }\nval drawing =\n    Img.zeros(440, 200, 3)\n        .drawFLines(\n            [ring(90.0, 100.0, 70.0, 64), ring(210.0, 105.0, 65.0, 3, -PI / 2), disc],\n            color = Vec4(1f, 1f, 1f, 1f),\n        )\nval ascii = ShapeAscii()\nshowAscii(\n    \"brightness\" to ascii.convert(drawing, 44, shape = false),\n    \"shape\" to ascii.convert(drawing, 44),\n)\n"}}} {"id" "ascii_shape_cube" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root"} "name" "Live cube in a charGrid" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [380.0 260.0 300.0 100.0] "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "ascii_shape_cube_notes_.md" "inline" "# Live, in a char grid\n\nA wireframe cube drawn into an Img every tick and matched by shape into a `charGrid` with `drawAscii`. Run to start, stop to stop.\n"} "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "ascii_shape_cube_code_.kt" "inline" "// A wireframe cube turning about two axes, drawn into an Img each tick and matched by shape.\nval ascii = ShapeAscii()\n// Corner i has x, y, z = ±1 from its three bits; an edge joins corners one bit apart.\nval corners =\n    (0 until 8).map { i ->\n        Triple(if (i and 1 == 0) -1.0 else 1.0, if (i and 2 == 0) -1.0 else 1.0, if (i and 4 == 0) -1.0 else 1.0)\n    }\nval edges = (0 until 8).flatMap { i -> [1, 2, 4].filter { i and it == 0 }.map { i to (i or it) } }\n\ncharGrid(cols = 60, rows = 26, glyphs = ascii.glyphs) {\n    val a = frame * 0.03\n    fun project(p: Triple<Double, Double, Double>): Pair<Double, Double> {\n        val (px, py, pz) = p\n        val x1 = px * cos(a) - pz * sin(a)\n        val z1 = px * sin(a) + pz * cos(a)\n        val y1 = py * cos(a * 0.7) - z1 * sin(a * 0.7)\n        val z2 = py * sin(a * 0.7) + z1 * cos(a * 0.7)\n        val s = 150.0 / (z2 + 4.0)\n        return (240 + x1 * s) to (130 + y1 * s)\n    }\n    val lines = edges.map { (i, j) ->\n        fline {\n            moveTo(project(corners[i]).first, project(corners[i]).second)\n            lineTo(project(corners[j]).first, project(corners[j]).second)\n            thickness = 5.0\n        }\n    }\n    val img = Img.zeros(480, 260, 3).drawFLines(lines, color = Vec4(1f, 1f, 1f, 1f))\n    drawAscii(ascii.convert(img, COLS, contrast = 3.0, rows = ROWS))\n}\n"}}} {"id" "ascii_shape_contrast" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root"} "name" "Contrast and directional contrast" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 260.0 300.0 100.0] "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "ascii_shape_contrast_notes_.md" "inline" "# Sharpening edges\n\n`contrast` and `directional` are exponents; 1 turns a step off. Compare the three rows.\n"} "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "ascii_shape_contrast_code_.kt" "inline" "// Three outlines and a filled disc, drawn white on black.\nfun ring(cx: Double, cy: Double, r: Double, sides: Int, turn: Double = 0.0) = fline {\n    for (i in 0..sides) {\n        val a = turn + 2 * PI * i / sides\n        if (i == 0) moveTo(cx + r * cos(a), cy + r * sin(a)) else lineTo(cx + r * cos(a), cy + r * sin(a))\n    }\n    thickness = 6.0\n}\nval disc = ring(360.0, 100.0, 55.0, 64).apply { filled = true }\nval drawing =\n    Img.zeros(440, 200, 3)\n        .drawFLines(\n            [ring(90.0, 100.0, 70.0, 64), ring(210.0, 105.0, 65.0, 3, -PI / 2), disc],\n            color = Vec4(1f, 1f, 1f, 1f),\n        )\nval ascii = ShapeAscii()\nshowAscii(\n    \"contrast 1\" to ascii.convert(drawing, 44),\n    \"contrast 3\" to ascii.convert(drawing, 44, contrast = 3.0),\n    \"contrast 3, directional 3\" to ascii.convert(drawing, 44, contrast = 3.0, directional = 3.0),\n    columns = 1,\n    cellSide = 600,\n)\n"}}}] "persistentProperties" ["frame" "name" "code" "code_language" "contents_language" "default_property" "file_proxy_mode" "file_proxy_path" "file_proxy_original_path" "file_proxy_mime" "filename" "preamble" "introduction" "attic" "notes" "geometryReviews" "geometryAppearance" "fragment" "stackSL" "rectSL" "msl" "vertex" "vertex_fragment" "task" "mesh" "raygen" "miss" "closesthit" "anyhit" "intersection" "callable" "fragment_s" "vertex_s" "task_s" "mesh_s" "raygen_s" "miss_s" "closesthit_s" "anyhit_s" "intersection_s" "callable_s" "children" "parents" "compute" "compute_s" "customization" "source_id" "templateId" "_tombstone" "isRemoteJSRoot" "isPythonRoot" ".*_editorState" "metadata" "nested" "nestedIn" "playlist" "pauseList" "bookmarks" "drawing" "panes" "slideShow" "autorun" "layers" "layerFrames" "_controlGroupValues" "_controlMidi" "keyframeData" "keyframeInterpolants" "ai4_auto_name" "ai4_auto_name_signature" "ai4_chat_history" "ai4_chat_running" "ai4_chat_suspension" "ai4_session" "fileManagerAccessHistory" "kitRole"]}